WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.536
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.836 --> 00:00:09.037
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:15.971
Unit thirty-one: Result and Purpose Clauses. Today you will explain why you do something and what happens as a result.

4
00:00:16.271 --> 00:00:18.889
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:23.182
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.017 --> 00:00:25.111
In order to.

7
00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:28.256
In order to means for the purpose of.

8
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.803
I study in order to pass.

9
00:00:31.417 --> 00:00:34.046
Your turn. Say: In order to.

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.145
In order to.

11
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:39.942
So as to.

12
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.741
So as to means with the purpose of.

13
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.640
We left early so as to avoid traffic.

14
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.891
Your turn. Say: So as to.

15
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:52.781
So as to.

16
00:00:53.517 --> 00:00:54.483
So that.

17
00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:57.135
So that means in order that.

18
00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.738
I wrote it so that I wouldn't forget.

19
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.724
Your turn. Say: So that.

20
00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:06.568
So that.

21
00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:08.434
In order that.

22
00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.251
In order that means a formal purpose conjunction.

23
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:14.629
In order that you may understand...

24
00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:17.660
Your turn. Say: In order that.

25
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:21.548
In order that.

26
00:01:22.283 --> 00:01:23.226
Purpose.

27
00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.379
Purpose means the reason you do something.

28
00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:28.275
What's the purpose?

29
00:01:28.883 --> 00:01:31.245
Your turn. Say: Purpose.

30
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.171
Purpose.

31
00:01:35.917 --> 00:01:36.767
Result.

32
00:01:37.783 --> 00:01:40.003
Result means what happens afterwards.

33
00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:42.117
The result was good.

34
00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:44.963
Your turn. Say: Result.

35
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:48.789
Result.

36
00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:50.319
So.

37
00:01:51.317 --> 00:01:53.444
So means introduces a result.

38
00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.841
It rained, so we stayed.

39
00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.615
Your turn. Say: So.

40
00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:02.282
So.

41
00:02:03.017 --> 00:02:03.844
Therefore.

42
00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.524
Therefore means as a result.

43
00:02:07.117 --> 00:02:09.093
He is ill; therefore he can't come.

44
00:02:09.683 --> 00:02:11.987
Your turn. Say: Therefore.

45
00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:15.927
Therefore.

46
00:02:16.733 --> 00:02:20.477
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.317 --> 00:02:25.908
Visal, join with so that: I set an alarm. I want to wake up early.

48
00:02:27.017 --> 00:02:37.239
I set an alarm so that I can wake up early. So that introduces a clause of purpose with a subject and a verb, often with can, could or would.

49
00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:39.815
What about in order to?

50
00:02:40.917 --> 00:02:55.158
In order to and so as to are followed by the infinitive: She studies hard in order to pass. We left early so as not to miss the train. In order that is more formal: in order that you may understand.

51
00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:57.959
How is that different from result?

52
00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:13.141
Result: It was late, so we took a taxi, or It rained; therefore the match stopped. So and therefore show the effect of what has happened. Purpose looks ahead; result looks back at what happened.

53
00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.137
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:16.983 --> 00:03:20.202
Grammar focus: Purpose and result clauses.

55
00:03:20.502 --> 00:03:21.747
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.879
I set an alarm so that I can wake up early.

57
00:03:25.783 --> 00:03:28.329
She studies hard in order to pass the exam.

58
00:03:29.217 --> 00:03:31.274
It was late, so we took a taxi.

59
00:03:32.233 --> 00:03:40.508
So that + clause (can / could / would). In order to / so as to + infinitive (so as not to for negatives). So / therefore = result.

60
00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.483
Be careful! Don't say: I study for to pass.

61
00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:48.677
Say: I study in order to pass.

62
00:03:48.977 --> 00:03:50.280
Use in order to.

63
00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:54.137
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:54.933 --> 00:03:56.457
Why and What Happened.

65
00:03:56.757 --> 00:03:59.279
I set an alarm so that I can wake up early.

66
00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:03.207
She studies hard in order to pass the final exam.

67
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.606
We left early so as not to miss the train.

68
00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.565
It was late, so we took a taxi.

69
00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:13.031
The result was that everyone arrived on time.

70
00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:18.193
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.212
I wrote it down blank I wouldn't forget.

72
00:04:21.512 --> 00:04:25.862
A, so that. B, in order to. C, so as.

73
00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.469
The answer is A: so that.

74
00:04:32.617 --> 00:04:34.825
He studies blank pass the exam.

75
00:04:35.125 --> 00:04:38.988
A, so that to. B, for. C, in order to.

76
00:04:42.533 --> 00:04:44.765
The answer is C: in order to.

77
00:04:45.917 --> 00:04:48.009
We left early blank miss the train.

78
00:04:48.309 --> 00:04:52.798
A, so as not to. B, so as to not. C, in order no.

79
00:04:56.333 --> 00:04:58.670
The answer is A: so as not to.

80
00:04:59.817 --> 00:05:01.259
Which shows result?

81
00:05:01.559 --> 00:05:07.534
A, I study to pass.. B, We left so that we could.. C, It was late, so we took a taxi..

82
00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.667
The answer is C: It was late, so we took a taxi..

83
00:05:15.817 --> 00:05:18.977
According to the reading, why did they leave early?

84
00:05:19.277 --> 00:05:23.697
A, not to miss the train. B, to buy tickets. C, to eat.

85
00:05:27.233 --> 00:05:29.895
The answer is A: not to miss the train.

86
00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:34.321
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:35.183 --> 00:05:39.313
Join with 'so that': 'I set an alarm. I want to wake up early.'

88
00:05:48.117 --> 00:05:49.629
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:49.929 --> 00:06:00.351
I set an alarm so that I can wake up early. I want to have time for breakfast, so I get up at six. So that shows the purpose, and so shows the result.

90
00:06:00.651 --> 00:06:02.325
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:03.217 --> 00:06:07.785
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and purpose and result clauses.

92
00:06:08.085 --> 00:06:12.722
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

93
00:06:13.022 --> 00:06:15.895
See you in Unit thirty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:16.195 --> 00:06:19.173
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

